==============================================================
=/                 C O N T R I B U T I N G                  \=
==============================================================


--[ 1. BEFORE YOU START ]--------------------------------------

VPort is deliberately small. A change that makes the server
bigger, slower or less predictable needs a very good reason.
If you plan something large, describe it to the maintainers
(see CREDITS) before writing the code.


--[ 2. CODE RULES ]--------------------------------------------

  Language   All code, program messages, error messages and
             commit messages are written in English.

  Comments   Source code is kept free of comments. Names must
             carry the meaning.

  Style      Run "cargo fmt" before committing. The tree must
             build without warnings.

  Tests      Run "cargo test". New protocol behaviour comes
             with a test in vport-proto.

  Unsafe     Allowed only for system calls, kept in small
             wrappers, never in protocol parsing.

  Memory     Every resource a client can cause the server to
             allocate must have a hard limit.

  Deps       No async runtime. New dependencies need a clear
             justification; today vportd uses only libc, plus
             sdl2 behind an optional feature.


--[ 3. PROTOCOL CHANGES ]--------------------------------------

  The VPort protocol is defined by protocol/PROTOCOL, not by
  any implementation. The code in this tree (vport-proto,
  libvport, vportd) follows the specification, never the other
  way around.

  A change to an opcode, a payload layout or a limit must
  update protocol/PROTOCOL in the same commit, and must bump
  PROTOCOL_VERSION when it is not backward compatible.

  The server must treat every byte from a client as hostile.
  A malformed frame disconnects that client and nothing else.


--[ 4. COMMITS ]-----------------------------------------------

  One logical change per commit. Subject line in English, in
  the imperative, up to 72 characters, with a prefix:

      feat:      new functionality
      fix:       bug fix
      refactor:  change without behaviour difference
      docs:      documentation only
      test:      tests only
      build:     Cargo and build system

  Example:

      feat: add in-memory backend with PPM dump


--[ 5. SENDING PATCHES AND BUG REPORTS ]-----------------------

  Send them to the developers listed in CREDITS. For a bug,
  include the vportd log, the client code that triggers it and
  the output of "uname -a".


==============================================================
